    {
      "id": "tiered-approval-and-sla",
      "name": "Tiered human approval, adverse action, and the idle register",
      "story": "As a credit officer I approve, decline with a controlled adverse-action reason, or return a deal from its dossier, with approval authority enforced server-side by exposure tier so an analyst cannot approve above $250,000, and I watch the SLA idle register for deals sitting more than five business days so I can reassign them.",
